\"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793820403442443001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f46e0592-047c-460d-b368-b5974eb61fb3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"20e1-f766-929b-4951"},{"link_uuid":"6c473d68-fd4d-4526-907e-e1021384f015","relation":"duplicates","target_id":"cded-334b-a742-4082"}],"description":"## Observation\nDuring a full `make verify` (default tier, PYTEST_WORKERS=4) on 2026-11-04 PST, 2 tests failed on worker gw0, while the same `tests/interfaces/facades` directory run alone passed (815 passed, 4 skipped):\n- tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py::test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr\n- tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py::test_cli_llm_error_is_clean_exit_one\n\nIn both, the captured stderr began with `--- Logging error ---` and a traceback ending in `ValueError: I/O operation on closed file`, raised from `logging/__init__.py` `emit`. The record being emitted was the authorship warning at `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:357` (\"signing SKIPPED ... no resolvable identity (author_id) for this writer; writing unsigned\"). The tests assert byte-identical stderr or \"no Traceback\", so the stray logging-error text fails them.\n\n## Hypothesis (unconfirmed)\n`install_stderr_handler` (`src/rebar/_logging.py:64`) binds `logging.StreamHandler(sys.stderr)` once and is idempotent by marker. When an earlier in-process `main()` call on the same worker installs it while `sys.stderr` is a pytest capture stream, that stream is later closed and the idempotency check never rebinds it, so later warnings write to a closed file. Order-dependent, so it shows only in full parallel runs.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction (two tests run in a fixed order in one process) shows the logging error before the fix.\n- [ ] After the fix, that reproduction passes and both listed tests pass in a full `make verify`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4c58-45d4-aaf7-48dc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Stale rebar stderr log handler writes to a closed capture stream across tests","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a91f9880-c426-4265-9909-9b3413b5c71b","f46e0592-047c-460d-b368-b5974eb61fb3","6c473d68-fd4d-4526-907e-e1021384f015"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793826055552828255,"uuid":"6fd4e929-8e1a-4f9d-acb3-83f79f96e713"}